<title>EGYPT: Arab Drugs profits soar in 1995/6.</title>
<headline>Arab Drugs profits soar in 1995/6.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net after-tax profits of Arab Drugs and Chemical Industries jumped 34.31 percent to 6.842 million pounds in the financial year 1995/6, from 5.094 million in 1994/5, according to audited results made available on Monday. The years end on June 30.</p>
<p>Profits before tax rose to 8.398 million from 6.600 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>Turnover was 94.125 million pounds, up from 85.222 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>The state sold the private sector 30 percent, or some 360,000 shares, of the company at 40.00 pounds a share. The shares were listed on Sunday.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.4 pounds</p>
<p>-- Esmat Salaheddin +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
